**Diagram to draw (large, side or front view):** with ruled label lines:

- two **testes** (singular: testis) in the **scrotum**, where sperms are made in the seminiferous tubules;
- the **epididymis** (coiled tube on each testis) where sperms are stored and mature;
- the **sperm duct (vas deferens)** leading from the epididymis up and over the bladder;
- the **seminal vesicle** and the **prostate gland**, which add fluids to the sperms (semen); optionally the Cowper's (bulbourethral) gland;
- the **urinary bladder** with the **ureter** entering it;
- the **urethra**, which carries both urine and semen, running through the **penis** and opening to the outside;
- the **penis** (with its glans), and the **scrotum** as the sac around the testes.

Title: *Male reproductive system of a mammal.*
